Project provenance
The early Rust implementation was developed with reference to the behavior and
design of Golalink (https://github.com/Golalink-Devs/Golalink). This attribution
records that history. The current service uses its own Rustlink API, track token
format, Rust client, and Discord voice implementation. Historical protocol
compatibility is not part of the current product.

Discord voice and DAVE
The Rustlink DAVE controller and Opus sender implement the published protocol:
  https://daveprotocol.com/
  https://github.com/discord/dave-protocol
MLS operations are provided by OpenMLS (MIT), and cryptographic primitives by
RustCrypto libraries under their respective licenses. No affiliation with or
endorsement by Discord is implied.

Tests use davey 0.1.5 (MIT) as an independent interoperability peer, and the sender
ratchet test vector published with its hash_ratchet tests:
  https://github.com/Snazzah/davey
The davey dependency is used only for tests, not by the production service.

Other dependencies and optional media tools retain their own licenses. Refer to
Cargo.lock, package metadata, and the upstream distributions of libopus and
FFmpeg for their attribution and distribution terms.
